WEBVTT

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:05.370
in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit. Amen.

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:12.370
The reading from the Sinaxarion for October 8, on which we commemorate,

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:20.220
our righteous mother, Belaya, the penitent. On the 8th of the month,

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:27.220
we celebrate the memory of our holy mother, Belaya, the repentant harlot.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:33.220
Saint Belaya lived at Antioch in the second half of the 5th century,

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:37.220
where she was the best known harlot of that great city.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:42.220
Her devotion to dancing and unchased pleasures made her a great fortune

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:47.220
that she spent entirely on adorning her body with costly raiment

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:54.220
and voluptuous perfumes in order to attract new victims into her net.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:59.220
She had many slaves and servants who ascorted her whenever,

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:04.220
seated in a luxurious chariot she went about the city.

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:12.470
One day, the Archbishop of Antioch invited Nonus, the holy bishop of Odessa,

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:17.470
to address some of his bishops in the Church of St. Julian.

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:22.470
For he was a man of inspired utterance, able to bring those who heard him

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:26.470
to repentance and love of virtue.

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:31.720
It so happened that Belaya, with her usual retinue,

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:37.720
passed by the doors of the Church, near where Nonus was speaking.

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:41.720
While the other bishops and pious folk averted their eyes,

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:47.720
Nonus looked upon the woman and wept, saying to them,

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:52.720
Whoa unto us, lazy and careless people,

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:56.720
who will have to give an account at the day of judgment

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:02.720
for not having been as zealous and careful to please God

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:08.720
as this poor woman has been to adorn her body for fleeting pleasure.

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:12.720
And he prayed fervently to the Lord for her conversion.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:16.720
Belaya was among those who listened to Nonus

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:20.720
preached on the Holy Gospel at divine service the next day.

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:25.720
What he said about the last judgment and everlasting punishment

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:31.720
struck her like a rapier thrust to the heart and awoke in her

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:37.720
a love for the heavenly bridegroom which is the only true love.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:42.720
On her return to her palace, she wrote to the holy bishop

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:47.720
asking him to receive her and not to scorn her for her depravity.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:53.720
If he were a true disciple of him who came to call not the righteous

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:56.720
but sinners to repentance.

00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:01.720
Nonus answered that if she had truly resolved to repent

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:05.720
she should come to church and confess her offenses

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:08.720
before the whole congregation of clergy and people.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:14.720
Belaya seized the opportunity and hastened to the church,

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:18.720
forgetful of all her pride and pomp.

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:22.720
She threw herself at the feet of the bishop and begged him

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:27.720
for regeneration to eternal life in holy baptism,

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:33.720
lest the devil and habit draw her back again to sinful ways.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:38.720
The whole city of Antioch rejoiced at the baptism of Belaya,

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:43.720
a nun called Romana, undertook to guide her first steps

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:47.720
in spiritual warfare and the life of repentance.

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:51.720
And so, by prayer and the sign of the cross,

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:56.720
Belaya overcame the temptations to return to her sinful life

00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:00.720
that were not slow to make their appearance.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:05.720
Some days after her baptism, she gave away all her wealth

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:08.720
to the poor and freed her slaves.

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:13.720
Then, free of every worldly tie and clad like a poor woman

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:17.720
in rough clothing, she departed for the Holy Land,

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:23.720
unknown to all, to lead the ascetic life on the mount of olives.

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:27.720
She remained for many years in a little cell,

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:32.720
struggling each day against the passions that were deeply rooted in her body

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:37.720
and devoting all the care she had once taken over her outward appearance

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:42.720
to adorning her soul for everlasting life.

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:47.720
Despite her solitary life, Belaya's valiant spiritual struggle

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:52.720
became well known to the other ascetics of Palestine.

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:57.720
They did not know, however, that she was, in fact, a woman.

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:01.720
When the Holy Penitent gave up her soul in peace to God,

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:06.720
all the monks thereabouts gathered to venerate her holy relics

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:11.720
and they gave great glory to God when a disciple of Nonus

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:15.720
told them the true story of Belaya's life.

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:19.720
For it teaches all who are engulfed in the darkness of sin,

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:28.720
not to despair, but to set out courageously on the road of repentance.

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:32.720
Through the prayers of our Holy Father's O Lord,

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:37.720
Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us and save us.
